{
  "summary": "TxIndex and node::GetTransaction are modified to throw std::runtime_error on disk I/O failures, deserialization errors, and index corruption rather than returning null. In getrawtransaction, block availability is checked via CheckBlockDataAvailability before reading, distinguishing un-downloaded or pruned blocks from missing transactions. ProcessPSBT is also refactored to query GetTransaction directly instead of using a custom fallback search.",
  "problem": "When block data reads or index lookups fail due to filesystem I/O errors or index corruption, GetTransaction and TxIndex return empty results, causing RPC and REST endpoints (such as getrawtransaction and /rest/tx/) to falsely report confirmed transactions as missing. Additionally, getrawtransaction previously returned a generic 'Block not available' or 'No such transaction found' message when blocks were pruned or still downloading.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit fa5c96a112 explains: 'Reporting a confirmed transaction as missing is wrong, so properly return an error instead... a -txindex corruption may also point to a larger system corruption and it seems better to notify the user properly by throwing an exception.'",
    "Release notes doc/release-notes-35728.md notes that getrawtransaction, gettxoutproof, utxoupdatepsbt, descriptorprocesspsbt, and /rest/tx/<TX-HASH> now surface internal errors on corrupted data rather than reporting transactions missing or silently continuing."
