  "card": "This PR modifies TxIndex and node::GetTransaction to throw std::runtime_error on disk I/O, deserialization, and index corruption errors rather than returning null. Currently, disk read errors or corrupted txindex databases cause RPC and REST endpoints to report that confirmed transactions do not exist, masking hardware failures or unclean shutdowns. The change ensures endpoints like getrawtransaction, gettxoutproof, and /rest/tx/ return internal errors instead of false 'not found' replies, and uses CheckBlockDataAvailability to distinguish pruned or downloading blocks.",
